2) Two-pointer problem (ABC-C)
Shortest Subarray With Sum ≥ K

Given N, K, and an array A of positive integers, find the minimum length of a contiguous subarray whose sum is at least K. If none, output -1.

Input

N K
A0 A1 ... A(N-1)


Constraints: 1 ≤ N ≤ 2e5, 1 ≤ Ai ≤ 1e9, 1 ≤ K ≤ 1e18
Output: one integer

